            "title": "Revance agrees to lower take-private offer by Crown Labs",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "The lowered takeover price follows months of delay in the deal after Revance, which makes a rival to AbbVie's blockbuster product Botox, faced a dispute with its partner Teoxane.  As per the current agreement, Crown will buy all of Revance's outstanding shares for $3.10 per share, or $325.20 million according to Reuters' calculations.  Revance received a notice in September for breaching the maximum allowed buffer stock levels and not adequately promoting and selling Teoxane's dermal fillers, as required by their distribution agreement.",
